  "gdtfWorkflowIntro": "For each fixture, follow these 3 steps in order.",
  "gdtfWorkflowSearchTitle": "Research",
  "gdtfWorkflowSearchBody": "“Search” tab. Type the name of your fixture (ex: \"Spiider\", \"MAC Viper\", \"Q-10\"). The GDTF Share database contains 6000+ official fixtures validated by manufacturers. It's free, instant, and 100% reliable. Use FIRST for 90% of cases.",
  "gdtfWorkflowPdfTitle": "Generate from PDF",
  "gdtfWorkflowPdfBody": "If the search yields nothing, go to the \"Generate from PDF\" tab. Upload the PDF manual/datasheet — the AI extracts the DMX modes automatically. ⚠️ Important: enter the exact fixture name (as written in the manual), and if you add modes manually, use the exact DMX mode names — otherwise the AI won't find the right data. Works well on clean PDFs (Robe, Martin, etc.) and less well on scanned or Chinese-translated manuals.",
  "gdtfWorkflowManualTitle": "Manual addition/correction",
  "gdtfWorkflowManualBody": "When the AI ​​has finished the analysis, you arrive on the mode selection page. The “Add a mode manually” button is ALWAYS available at the top of the list. Use it to: (a) add a mode that the AI ​​forgot, (b) delete a hallucination via trash, (c) correct an incorrect channel count (trash + re-add to the correct number). This is your last line of defense before generating GDTF — always check.",
  "gdtfWorkflowTip": "Tip: before extracting a PDF, always check gdtf-share — this saves you from AI extraction (longer and less reliable) when an official GDTF already exists. And remember: fixture name and mode names must be exactly as in the manual — the AI depends on it!",
  "gdtfUnderstood": "Understood",
  "gdtfWorkflowSearchShortBody": "Type the fixture name above. GDTF Share database (6000+ official fixtures). It's free, instant, manufacturer validated. Solves 90% of cases.",
  "gdtfWorkflowPdfShortBody": "Not found? “Generate from PDF” tab. Upload the manual — the AI ​​extracts the DMX modes. Works best on clean PDFs.",
  "gdtfWorkflowManualShortBody": "On the modes page, always check what the AI ​​has output. You can: add a forgotten mode, delete an hallucination (trash icon), or correct a false channel count (delete + re-add to the correct value). The AI ​​is fast but not infallible — you remain in control of the final list.",
  "gdtfAddModeManually": "Add a mode manually",
  "gdtfNoModeDetectedAutomatically": "No mode detected automatically.",
  "gdtfNoModeDetectedHelp": "The PDF is probably scanned or with a complex layout. Add the modes manually with the button above, and the extraction of the channels will then be done on the OCR text / extracted from the manual.",
  "gdtfAddMode": "Add a mode",
