  "helpPageTitle": "Network Tools Guide",
  "helpIntro": "All tools operate in read-only mode on your local network. Tap a tool to see details.",
  "helpSectionDoes": "What it does",
  "helpSectionDelay": "Timing",
  "helpSectionLimits": "What it doesn't do",
  "helpSectionTip": "Tip",
  "helpGeneralTitle": "General tips",
  "helpGeneralSubnet": "All tools operate on the local /24 subnet. Devices on a different VLAN or behind a router will not be detected.",
  "helpGeneralFirewall": "Software firewalls may block certain probes. If devices are missing, check your filtering rules.",
  "helpGeneralWifi": "WiFi networks with client isolation block discovery. Prefer a wired connection or a WiFi in bridge mode.",
  "helpToolScanDoes": "Scans the /24 subnet in parallel and identifies active devices. Shows IP, hostname, manufacturer (via MAC OUI) and common open ports.",
  "helpToolScanDelay": "15 to 30 seconds depending on network size. 50 simultaneous probes.",
  "helpToolScanLimits": "Does not cross VLANs or routers. Does not perform full port scans or WAN scanning.",
  "helpToolScanTip": "If devices are missing, check that your firewall does not block incoming TCP/ICMP probes.",
  "helpToolDashboardDoes": "Shows real-time status of detected devices: availability, latency, active network alerts.",
  "helpToolDashboardDelay": "Updates every 30 seconds. First load is immediate after the scan.",
  "helpToolDashboardLimits": "Does not retain history between sessions. Requires a prior scan to populate the device list.",
  "helpToolDashboardTip": "Run a network scan before opening the dashboard to see all available devices.",
  "helpToolArtNetDoes": "Passively listens to Art-Net packets (UDP 6454) and displays active DMX universes with real-time values.",
  "helpToolArtNetDelay": "Real-time — data appears in under one second upon packet reception.",
  "helpToolArtNetLimits": "No DMX output. Does not configure Art-Net nodes and does not support the RDM protocol.",
  "helpToolArtNetTip": "Art-Net does not cross routers. All devices must be on the same L2 network (same switch or same segment).",
  "helpToolSacnDoes": "Listens to sACN/E1.31 multicast streams (UDP 5568) and displays active universes, source priorities and DMX values.",
  "helpToolSacnDelay": "Real-time — latency under one second.",
  "helpToolSacnLimits": "No DMX output. Does not modify priorities or sACN source configuration.",
  "helpToolSacnTip": "sACN multicast requires a managed switch with IGMP snooping enabled to prevent broadcast storms on the network.",
  "helpToolNdiDoes": "Detects NDI video sources on the LAN via the NDI discovery protocol. Shows name, IP address and type of each source.",
  "helpToolNdiDelay": "Sources appear 5 to 15 seconds after connecting to the network.",
  "helpToolNdiLimits": "No video playback or NDI routing. Does not detect NDI|HX sources without active mDNS discovery.",
  "helpToolNdiTip": "NDI requires a minimum of 100 Mb/s per stream. Avoid WiFi for production — prefer a Gigabit wired connection.",
  "helpToolDiagDoes": "Runs a series of network health tests: connectivity, DNS resolution, latency, packet loss and service availability.",
  "helpToolDiagDelay": "Full diagnostic in 20 to 30 seconds.",
  "helpToolDiagLimits": "Diagnostic only — no automatic repair, no configuration changes.",
  "helpToolDiagTip": "Run a diagnostic before and after a network change to compare state and quickly isolate regressions.",
  "helpToolSnapshotDoes": "Captures the network state at a point in time (devices, services) and lets you compare two snapshots to identify changes.",
  "helpToolSnapshotDelay": "Capture in 30 to 45 seconds depending on network size.",
  "helpToolSnapshotLimits": "No continuous monitoring or automatic alerts. History is stored on this device only.",
  "helpToolSnapshotTip": "Ideal for documenting state before/after an infrastructure change or isolating a regression during troubleshooting.",
  "helpToolLuminexDoes": "Queries Luminex GigaCore switches via their HTTP API. Shows port status (link, speed, PoE, errors), temperature, PSUs and triggers alarms.",
  "helpToolLuminexDelay": "Polling every 30 seconds. Auto-discovery on the subnet: 15 to 30 seconds.",
  "helpToolLuminexLimits": "Read-only. No VLAN, group or port configuration changes. Does not support MA-Net or NDI video.",
  "helpToolLuminexTip": "Default credentials: admin / empty password. Gen2 switches expose /api/v1/, Gen1 respond on /stat/ports as plain text.",
  "helpToolManetDoes": "Passively listens on UDP port 6549 and detects grandMA2/3 consoles and nodes broadcasting on the network. Shows name, device type, firmware version and MAC address.",
  "helpToolManetDelay": "Devices appear on their next network broadcast, typically within 10 seconds.",
  "helpToolManetLimits": "Read-only. No show data, no DMX values, no configuration. Does not cross VLANs.",
  "helpToolManetTip": "If no devices appear: check that grandMA is configured to broadcast on the LAN and that UDP port 6549 is not blocked by a firewall.",
